<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal Jan-Sept trade deficit 1,054 bln esc.</title>
<headline>Portugal Jan-Sept trade deficit 1,054 bln esc.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's global trade deficit fell to 1,054 billion escudos between January and September from 1,136 billion in same period last year, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>		   Jan-Sept 96 Jan-Sept 95</p>
<p> Overall balance  -1,054.4   -1,135.6</p>
<p> Imports	     3,788.8    3,697.9</p>
<p> Exports	     2,734.4    2,562.1</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in billions of escudos. A minus sign denotes a deficit. 1995 figures are definitive while 1996 figures are preliminary.</p>
<p>European Union trade</p>
<p>			   Jan-Sept 96  Jan-Sept 95</p>
<p> Overall balance     -632.9	    -683.4</p>
<p> Imports		 2,825.7	   2,753.2</p>
<p> Exports		 2,192.8	   2,069.9</p>
<p>Non-EU trade</p>
<p> Overall balance     -421.5	     -452.5</p>
<p> Imports		 963.1		 944.7</p>
<p> Exports		 541.6		 492.2</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom 3511-3538254</p>
</text>
